<title>CANADA: Canada October budget deficit shrinks sharply.</title>
<headline>Canada October budget deficit shrinks sharply.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's budget deficit narrowed sharply in October to C$0.5 billion from C$2.9 billion a year earlier, the Finance Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>The department said the year-over-year improvement reflected a C$2.0 billion increase in budgetary revenues, as well as a C$0.5 billion decline in program spending.</p>
<p>Over the first seven months of the fiscal year ending March 31, the deficit was C$7.5 billion, compared with C$17.62 billion in the same year-ago period.  </p>
<p>Budgetary transactions (in billions of dollars)</p>
<p>						  Oct 96     Oct 95</p>
<p>Revenues				     +12.08     +10.10</p>
<p>Deficit					 -0.50	-2.94</p>
<p>Program spending			    -8.75	-9.20</p>
<p>Operating balance			   +3.33	+0.91</p>
<p>Public debt charges			 -3.83	-3.85</p>
<p>Financial requirements (ex forex)     -0.15	-1.60</p>
<p>(Note: Positive numbers indicate net source of funds. Negative numbers indicate net requirement for funds.)  </p>
<p>Budgetary transactions (in billions of dollars)</p>
<p>				   Yr to date 96/97   Yr to date 95/96</p>
<p>Revenues				     +76.65     +70.79</p>
<p>Deficit					 -7.50     -17.62</p>
<p>Program spending			   -57.56     -61.05</p>
<p>Operating balance			  +19.09	+9.74</p>
<p>Public debt charges			-26.59     -27.36</p>
<p>Financial requirements (ex forex)     -4.40     -14.11</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
